**On deployments without Atlas Search, this code repeats full partition setup on every vector write.**

When `searchIndexStatus !== "ready"`, the code removes the setup promise from the memo. On a deployment without Atlas Search, `listSearchIndexes` always throws, so the status is always `"error"`. Each later call to `replaceMongoVectorEntries` or `upsertMongoVectorDocuments` then runs `materializeVectorPartition` again:
- an upsert and a `findOne` on `vector_partitions`,
- 11 `createIndex` calls,
- `reconcileManagedTtl`,
- the search-index probe and an `"error"` status write.

With TTL disabled (the default), `reconcileManagedTtl` also runs `updateMany({ expiresAt: { $exists: true } }, ...)` on the partition. Line 682 always stores `expiresAt: null`, so that update matches and rewrites every document in the partition on every write. See the `reconcileManagedTtl` finding in `packages/openplanner-sdk/src/mongodb.ts`.

On Atlas, an index that is still building makes each write wait in `waitForQueryableSearchIndex` for up to 60 s. That is longer than the 30 s `withTimeout` in `ingest.ts`.

Memoize the storage setup (collection and support indexes) separately from the search-index readiness. Retry only the search-index step, and limit how often it is retried.

